Based on the screenshot and the stack‐trace you’re seeing, the root cause is that in the extension context the raw trace often does *not* contain a “firstPaint” event, so this line in `trace-of-tab.js`:

```js
const firstPaint = frameEvents.find(e => e.name === 'firstPaint');
// …
const navigationStart = frameEvents
  .filter(e => e.name === 'navigationStart' && e.ts < firstPaint.ts)
  .pop();
```

blows up because `firstPaint` is `undefined` and you end up doing `undefined.ts`.

The fix is to fall back to `firstContentfulPaint` when `firstPaint` is missing – and, if there is still no paint event, simply grab the last `navigationStart` in the trace instead of always trying to compare against `firstPaint.ts`. Below is a *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch for exactly that in `lighthouse-core/gather/computed/trace-of-tab.js`.

